drills.solution:
Split the cross into three one-gene crosses and find each probability (a 2 × 2 Punnett square for each, or the gamete probabilities: AA gives A with probability 1, Aa gives A with probability $\tfrac12$, aa never gives A).

- Gene A, {a1} × {a2}: P({ta}) = {pa:frac}
- Gene B, {b1} × {b2}: P({tb}) = {pb:frac}
- Gene C, {c1} × {c2}: P({tc}) = {pc:frac}

The genes are independent, so multiply (product rule): ${pa:texfrac} \times {pb:texfrac} \times {pc:texfrac} =$ **{p:frac}**.

